From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: vdec: report the tallest frame the macroblock
 limit allows

VIDIOC_ENUM_FRAMESIZES reports the firmware's width and height limits,
but the decoder also has a macroblocks-per-frame limit, which a stepwise
range cannot express. On AR50_LITE (QCM2290/SM6115) the range is
128x128 - 1920x1920 while a frame may hold 8160 macroblocks (1920x1088).

A client that checks only the reported bounds takes the decoder for
streams it cannot decode. Chromium's V4L2 decoder does: it would send
Steam's 1920x1200 VP9 startup movies (9000 macroblocks) to venus, which
returns no frame and no error for them.

Report the tallest frame that fits at the widest width instead, so such
a stream goes to a software decoder. Portrait frames taller than that
leave the reported range, although the hardware could decode them.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
index 6a43ea1..df91fa5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -497,6 +497,7 @@ static int vdec_enum_framesizes(struct file *file, void *fh,
 {
 	struct venus_inst *inst = to_inst(file);
 	const struct venus_format *fmt;
+	u32 mbs, cols;
 
 	fmt = find_format(inst, fsize->pixel_format,
 			  V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE);
@@ -519,6 +520,18 @@ static int vdec_enum_framesizes(struct file *file, void *fh,
 	fsize->stepwise.max_height = frame_height_max(inst);
 	fsize->stepwise.step_height = frame_height_step(inst);
 
+	/*
+	 * The firmware also limits the macroblocks in a frame, which a stepwise
+	 * range cannot express. Report the tallest frame that fits at the widest
+	 * width, so that a client which checks only these bounds does not pick
+	 * the decoder for a frame it cannot decode: on AR50_LITE a 1920x1200
+	 * stream needs 9000 of its 8160 macroblocks and returns no frame at all.
+	 */
+	mbs = mbs_per_frame_max(inst);
+	cols = DIV_ROUND_UP(fsize->stepwise.max_width, 16);
+	if (mbs && cols && mbs / cols * 16 < fsize->stepwise.max_height)
+		fsize->stepwise.max_height = mbs / cols * 16;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
